Input: {"question": "Which award did Jean-René Roy receive?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 96, "text": "**Renowned Canadian Astronomer Honored with Prestigious Knight of the National Order of Quebec**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 98, "end": 322, "text": "Montreal, Quebec - In a ceremony held at the Quebec National Assembly, Canadian astronomer Jean-René Roy was bestowed the esteemed title of Knight of the National Order of Quebec, the highest honor conferred by the province."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 323, "end": 485, "text": "This prestigious recognition acknowledges Roy's outstanding contributions to the field of astronomy and his dedication to promoting scientific literacy in Canada."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 486, "end": 715, "text": "The National Order of Quebec, established in 1984, is the highest distinction awarded by the Quebec government to individuals who have made significant contributions to the province's cultural, scientific, and social development."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 716, "end": 859, "text": "The Knight rank, the first of three levels, is reserved for those who have demonstrated exceptional achievements and commitment to their field."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 860, "end": 1014, "text": "Jean-René Roy, a respected figure in the Canadian astronomical community, has spent decades studying the universe and sharing his passion with the public."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1015, "end": 1183, "text": "His groundbreaking research on star formation and galaxy evolution has earned him international recognition, with numerous publications in esteemed scientific journals."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1184, "end": 1282, "text": "\"Jean-René Roy is an exceptional scientist and a true ambassador for Canadian astronomy,\" said Dr."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1283, "end": 1338, "text": "Victoria Kaspi, Director of the McGill Space Institute."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1339, "end": 1471, "text": "\"His tireless efforts to promote science education and outreach have inspired countless students and enthusiasts across the country."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1472, "end": 1546, "text": "This honor is a well-deserved recognition of his remarkable achievements.\""}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1547, "end": 1664, "text": "Roy's commitment to science communication has been instrumental in making astronomy accessible to a broader audience."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1665, "end": 1803, "text": "He has written several popular science books, hosted television documentaries, and developed educational programs for schools and museums."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1804, "end": 2026, "text": "\"Jean-René Roy's work has not only advanced our understanding of the universe but has also inspired a new generation of scientists and science enthusiasts,\" said Quebec Minister of Culture and Communications, Nathalie Roy."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2027, "end": 2191, "text": "\"His dedication to promoting scientific literacy and critical thinking is a testament to his exceptional character and commitment to the betterment of our society.\""}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2192, "end": 2459, "text": "According to the National Order of Quebec's official website, Roy's induction into the Order is a testament to his \"outstanding contributions to the development of astronomy in Quebec and Canada, as well as his commitment to promoting science education and outreach.\""}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2460, "end": 2635, "text": "Data from the National Order of Quebec reveals that since its inception, only a select few have been awarded the Knight rank, making Roy's achievement all the more remarkable."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2636, "end": 2770, "text": "In a statement, Roy expressed his gratitude for the honor, saying, \"I am humbled and grateful to receive this prestigious recognition."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2771, "end": 2886, "text": "I hope that this award will inspire others to pursue careers in science and to share their passion with the world.\""}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 13, "text": "Jean-René Roy"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 15, "end": 124, "text": "Jean-René Roy is a Canadian astronomer renowned for his groundbreaking research in the field of astrophysics."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 125, "end": 280, "text": "Born on February 12, 1965, in Montreal, Quebec, Canada, Roy has made significant contributions to the understanding of celestial bodies and their behavior."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 281, "end": 305, "text": "Early Life and Education"}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 307, "end": 414, "text": "Roy pursued his undergraduate degree in physics from McGill University, graduating magna cum laude in 1987."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 415, "end": 448, "text": "He then went on to earn his Ph.D."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 449, "end": 530, "text": "in astronomy from the University of Toronto in 1992, under the supervision of Dr."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 531, "end": 542, "text": "John Smith."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 543, "end": 549, "text": "Career"}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 551, "end": 663, "text": "Roy's research focuses on the study of binary star systems and their applications in understanding the universe."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 664, "end": 795, "text": "He has published numerous papers in esteemed scientific journals, including the Astrophysical Journal and the Astronomical Journal."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 796, "end": 813, "text": "Awards and Honors"}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 815, "end": 935, "text": "In 1995, Roy was awarded the prestigious Fulbright Scholarship, a highly competitive American educational grant program."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 936, "end": 1126, "text": "This recognition enabled him to conduct research at the Harvard-Smithsonian Center for Astrophysics, where he collaborated with prominent astronomers and expanded his knowledge in the field."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1127, "end": 1147, "text": "Studies and Research"}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1149, "end": 1261, "text": "During his Fulbright tenure, Roy conducted a comprehensive study on the orbital dynamics of binary star systems."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1262, "end": 1435, "text": "His research, published in the journal Science in 1997, provided new insights into the stability of these systems and their potential applications in astrophysical research."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1436, "end": 1575, "text": "In 2001, Roy was part of an international team that discovered a new binary star system, which was later named \"Roy's Binary\" in his honor."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1576, "end": 1690, "text": "This discovery was published in the journal Nature and garnered significant attention in the scientific community."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1691, "end": 1701, "text": "References"}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1703, "end": 1754, "text": "* \"Jean-René Roy: A Rising Star in Astronomy\" by J."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1755, "end": 1788, "text": "Johnson, Astronomy Magazine, Vol."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1789, "end": 1796, "text": "23, No."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1797, "end": 1804, "text": "4, 1996"}, "D2S25": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1805, "end": 1885, "text": "* \"Fulbright Scholars: A Legacy of Excellence\" by the Fulbright Commission, 2002"}, "D2S26": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1886, "end": 1938, "text": "* \"Orbital Dynamics of Binary Star Systems\" by J.-R."}, "D2S27": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1939, "end": 1957, "text": "Roy, Science, Vol."}, "D2S28": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1958, "end": 1966, "text": "276, No."}, "D2S29": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1967, "end": 1977, "text": "5315, 1997"}, "D2S30": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1978, "end": 2028, "text": "* \"Discovery of a New Binary Star System\" by J.-R."}, "D2S31": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2029, "end": 2053, "text": "Roy et al., Nature, Vol."}, "D2S32": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2054, "end": 2062, "text": "412, No."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Fulbright Scholarship", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Jean-René Roy", "scope": "Awards and Honors", "claim": "In 1995, Roy was awarded the prestigious Fulbright Scholarship.", "answer": "Fulbright Scholarship", "quote": "In 1995, Roy was awarded the prestigious Fulbright Scholarship, a highly competitive American educational grant program.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["Knight of the National Order of Quebec", "Fulbright Scholarship"]}
